# Every variable the engine reads (DEPLOYMENT.md §8), grouped, with safe local
# defaults — no real secret is ever a good default, so live values only ever
# come from `.env.local` (gitignored) or, on a server, Infisical → shared/.env
# (DEPLOYMENT.md §8, CONVENTIONS.md §13). Copy this file to `.env.local` and
# fill in what your task needs; `pnpm worktree`/`worktree:env` (1.3, 3.3) writes
# PORT, DB_SUFFIX and a fresh development LINK_TOKEN_KEYS ring into it for you.
# `bootCheck()` (@engine/config/boot-check) reads this environment at process
# start and refuses to start on a missing or malformed value — on a workstation
# a missing provider or storage secret is only a warning.

# --- This worktree (written by `pnpm worktree`/`worktree:env`, TASKS.md 1.3) --
# PORT       this worktree's dev server port, unique per (phase, lane)
# DB_SUFFIX  this worktree's database suffix — `pnpm db:fresh` names its
#            database <brand>_<DB_SUFFIX>, so two worktrees never share one
#            (engine/tooling/db)
PORT=
DB_SUFFIX=

# --- Brand selection (BRANDS.md §1-2) ---
# BRAND            indies-gallery | old-east-indies | test
# BRAND_ROOT       the brand folder: the one holding site/ (the loader reads
#                  <BRAND_ROOT>/site/brand.config.json, copy/ and assets/).
#                  Locally, the repo-root brand folder (./test, ./indies-gallery);
#                  on a host, the release's `brand` folder beside its build:
#                  BRAND_ROOT=<current>/brand, where the release holds
#                  brand/site/ and engine/apps/<app>/server.js (DEPLOYMENT.md §8,
#                  .github/scripts/assemble-artifact.sh)
# TEST_STOREFRONT  CI / the `test` brand only: gallery | emporium — which of
#                  its two configs to load
BRAND=test
BRAND_ROOT=./test
TEST_STOREFRONT=gallery

# --- Payload / the app (DEPLOYMENT.md §8) ---
# DATABASE_URL      postgres://<user>:<password>@<host>:<port>/<database> —
#                   built from the Postgres block below for local dev; a
#                   server's is the brand's own database (ig_db, oei_db)
# PAYLOAD_SECRET    signs Payload's sessions and tokens: Payload refuses to
#                   start without one. Any long random string locally; a real
#                   secret of its own per brand and environment on a server.
#                   No repo tool needs yours: `pnpm db:fresh`'s migrate and
#                   `pnpm check:generated`'s generators hand Payload their own
#                   placeholder (they sign nothing) and never see this one
# SITE_URL          the app's own origin, for absolute URLs and CSP. It also
#                   decides the environment bootCheck() applies: the brand's
#                   domains.production (or an alias) is production, its
#                   domains.staging is staging, a dev server is local (sandbox
#                   keys, fixtures allowed) — and a production build at a
#                   loopback host is local only with LOCAL_PRODUCTION_BUILD=1
# LOCAL_PRODUCTION_BUILD
#                   1 or blank, nothing else. 1 lets a production build
#                   (`next build` + `next start`) at a loopback SITE_URL
#                   (localhost, *.localhost, 127.0.0.1, [::1]) run as local —
#                   how a worktree and CI open one on their own port, with
#                   draft configs and sandbox keys; without it that build is
#                   judged production and refused (DEPLOYMENT.md §8). Set to 1
#                   ONLY in a worktree's .env.local (`pnpm worktree:env`
#                   writes it, and never overwrites a value) and in CI's jobs
#                   that start a production build — NEVER in a host's
#                   shared/.env; on a brand's own domain it is ignored
# NODE_ENV          set by Next itself — "production" for `next build`/`start`
# HOSTNAME          the address a production server binds (`node server.js`,
#                   Next's standalone server). 0.0.0.0 — or localhost — and
#                   NEVER a loopback IP: at 127.0.0.1 Next's router calls its own
#                   origin 127.0.0.1 while the proxy's request URL says
#                   localhost, so every rewrite looks external and each page
#                   hangs (TASKS.md 4.4.g). Pin it on a host: Linux shells and
#                   containers export their machine name as HOSTNAME, which
#                   the server would otherwise bind. A bind address, never an
#                   origin — SITE_URL is the origin. `next dev`/`next start`
#                   take -H instead, so a worktree leaves it commented out
# RUN_MIGRATIONS    1 in the web process only (DEPLOYMENT.md §2-4): its first
#                   getPayload() applies pending migrations under an advisory
#                   lock. Payload does that only in a production build, so it
#                   takes RUN_MIGRATIONS=1 AND NODE_ENV=production (`next
#                   start`); a dev server with RUN_MIGRATIONS=1 migrates
#                   nothing. Never set locally: `pnpm db:fresh --brand <slug>`
#                   migrates the database it makes (`pnpm --filter @engine/cms
#                   migrate`, TASKS.md 3.5.c)
# PAYLOAD_DEV_PUSH  1 lets Payload's dev push write the whole schema straight
#                   into a database with no migration: for a SCHEMA AUTHOR's
#                   own suffixed database only, never a production build
#                   (Payload ignores it there), and never with a migration
#                   committed from it (PARALLEL-TRACKS.md §3.2). Anyone else
#                   boots on a database `pnpm db:fresh` migrated. Should a
#                   push fail on a database that has tables, push onto an
#                   empty one: `pnpm db:fresh --brand <slug> --no-migrate`.
#                   A pushed database lacks what only a migration carries (a
#                   trigger, raw SQL), so tests of those run on a migrated one.
#                   Left unset
DATABASE_URL=
PAYLOAD_SECRET=dev-only-not-a-secret
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
LOCAL_PRODUCTION_BUILD=
RUN_MIGRATIONS=
PAYLOAD_DEV_PUSH=
# HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0

# --- Loaders (DESIGN-SYSTEM.md §3, bootCheck) ---
# LOADERS_SOURCE  payload (the default, when unset) | fixtures — where the
#                 apps' loaders read view models from. `fixtures` renders the
#                 committed fixtures with no catalogue in the database; it is
#                 refused in production and warned about in staging.
LOADERS_SOURCE=

# --- Capability links' key ring (C6 links, DEPLOYMENT.md §8) ---
# LINK_TOKEN_KEYS  comma-separated entries:
#                    kid:secret             the ONE current key (derives new links)
#                    kid:secret:YYYY-MM-DD  retired that UTC day; still verifies
#                                           for LINK_TOKEN.keyOverlapDays
#                    kid:revoked            refuses at once (a leaked key)
#                  a kid is 1-12 of a-z/0-9 and never reused; a secret is
#                  base64url of >= 32 RANDOM bytes — base64url only, never
#                  standard base64 (`+`, `/`: `openssl rand -base64` writes
#                  that one, and C1 refuses it) — not a password, not a
#                  pattern (C6's test-vector key is refused). One ring per
#                  brand and per environment, never shared; a restart applies a
#                  change. Left blank here on purpose: `pnpm worktree:env`
#                  writes a fresh `dev:<32 random bytes>` ring into .env.local
#                  when it has none, and never overwrites one. By hand:
#                    node -e "console.log('dev:'+require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
LINK_TOKEN_KEYS=

# --- Local Postgres (docker-compose.dev.yml, engine/tooling/db) ---
# Read by `pnpm db:fresh`/`db:drop`/`db:list`/`pnpm schema-hash` to reach
# Postgres through `docker compose exec` by default — not part of
# DEPLOYMENT.md §8's server-side list, but every worktree needs the same
# defaults to talk to one shared container.
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432

# --- The CMS's real-database tests (engine/packages/cms/**/*.db.test.ts) ---
# CMS_TEST_POSTGRES_URL  a Postgres server's maintenance database, as a role
#                        that may CREATE DATABASE — each test makes its own
#                        database there, migrates it and drops it after, e.g.
#                        postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/postgres
#                        for the local stack. Unset, those tests skip (so
#                        `pnpm test` needs no database); CI's e2e job sets it.
#                        Never a brand's database, never a server's.
# CMS_TEST_POSTGRES_URL=

# --- Direct Postgres transport (engine/tooling/db/transport.mjs) ---
# Leave unset locally — `docker compose exec` (above) is what a worktree
# wants. Setting PGHOST switches `psql.mjs`/`schema-hash/dump.mjs` to a plain
# `psql`/`pg_dump` on PATH instead, connecting to PGHOST:PGPORT directly —
# CI's e2e job sets these because its Postgres is a bare service container
# with no compose project for `exec` to reach (TASKS.md 2.3.a). PGPASSWORD is
# read by `psql`/`pg_dump` themselves, never passed on a command line.
# PGHOST=
# PGPORT=5432
# PGPASSWORD=
# PG_TRANSPORT=   # 'direct' or 'compose' to force a transport instead of
#                 # inferring it from PGHOST

# --- Media storage (S3-compatible; MinIO locally, DEPLOYMENT.md §2) ---
# S3_ENDPOINT                object storage endpoint (MinIO locally)
# S3_BUCKET                  the brand's public media bucket: ig-media |
#                            oei-media | test-media (2.1.a bootstraps all three)
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID / SECRET  MinIO's root user locally; a scoped key on a server
# S3_REGION                  optional: the bucket's region. Unset, the storage
#                            adapter sends "auto" — what R2 takes, and MinIO
#                            (no region configured) accepts; set it only for
#                            a store that insists on one
# MEDIA_PUBLIC_URL           the CDN/base URL media is served from
# MASTERS_BUCKET             archive-masters (private; OEI's key writes only
#                            under print-files/ there — DEPLOYMENT.md §2)
# MASTERS_ACCESS_KEY_ID / SECRET
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
S3_BUCKET=test-media
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin
# S3_REGION=
MEDIA_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:9000/test-media
MASTERS_BUCKET=archive-masters
MASTERS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=minioadmin
MASTERS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=minioadmin

# --- Mail (Mailpit locally, docker-compose.dev.yml) ---
SMTP_HOST=localhost
SMTP_PORT=1025
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
SMTP_FROM_ADDRESS=dev@example.test
SMTP_FROM_NAME="Indies Platform (dev)"

# --- Provider secrets (DEPLOYMENT.md §8, PAYMENTS.md §8) ---
# Which variables exist follows the brand config, so none is set here. The
# names are the ones bootCheck() reads (@engine/config/boot-check,
# provider-secrets.ts): seller and provider ids upper-cased, `-` as `_`.
#   PAYMENT_<SELLER>_<PROVIDER>_<NAME>   per seller, per payment provider
#   SHIPPING_<SELLER>_<PROVIDER>_<NAME>  per seller too — a shipping webhook
#                                        is per seller, like a payment one
#   FULFILMENT_<PROVIDER>_<NAME>         per brand: fulfilment has no seller
# A seller's shipping secrets follow its OWN `sellers[].shipping` in the brand
# config (C1 v1.2) — every one of the brand's `shipping.providers` when it names
# none — so a seller shipping its own stock by DHL Express needs no Biteship
# key, and bootCheck() asks for none.
# Sandbox vs live: Stripe, Midtrans and Xendit keys say which they are
# (sk_test_/sk_live_, SB-Mid-/Mid-, xnd_development_/xnd_production_); the
# providers whose keys cannot say it take `<PREFIX>_MODE=sandbox|live`.
# Production runs live keys, staging and local sandbox keys; any other
# pairing, or sandbox and live mixed under one prefix, refuses the boot.
#
#   provider (kind)          secrets (<PREFIX>_…)                          _MODE
#   stripe (payment)         SECRET_KEY PUBLISHABLE_KEY WEBHOOK_SECRET     no
#   midtrans (payment)       SERVER_KEY CLIENT_KEY                         no
#   xendit (payment)         SECRET_KEY WEBHOOK_TOKEN                      no
#   paypal (payment)         CLIENT_ID CLIENT_SECRET WEBHOOK_ID            yes
#   doku (payment)           CLIENT_ID SECRET_KEY                          yes
#   manual, bank-transfer    none
#   biteship (shipping)      API_KEY WEBHOOK_SECRET                        yes
#   dhl-express (shipping)   API_KEY API_SECRET ACCOUNT_NUMBER             yes
#   flat, quote, collect     none
#   prodigi (fulfilment)     API_KEY                                       yes
#   gelato (fulfilment)      API_KEY                                       yes
#   own-stock, local-production  none
#
# e.g. for a seller "id" on Midtrans and Biteship, and Prodigi print-on-demand:
# PAYMENT_ID_MIDTRANS_SERVER_KEY=
# PAYMENT_ID_MIDTRANS_CLIENT_KEY=
# SHIPPING_ID_BITESHIP_API_KEY=
# SHIPPING_ID_BITESHIP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# SHIPPING_ID_BITESHIP_MODE=sandbox
# FULFILMENT_PRODIGI_API_KEY=
# FULFILMENT_PRODIGI_MODE=sandbox
# and for a seller "sg" on PayPal and DHL Express:
# PAYMENT_SG_PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
# PAYMENT_SG_PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# PAYMENT_SG_PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=
# PAYMENT_SG_PAYPAL_MODE=sandbox
# SHIPPING_SG_DHL_EXPRESS_API_KEY=
# SHIPPING_SG_DHL_EXPRESS_API_SECRET=
# SHIPPING_SG_DHL_EXPRESS_ACCOUNT_NUMBER=
# SHIPPING_SG_DHL_EXPRESS_MODE=sandbox

# --- WhatsApp and the sister-storefront sync ---
# WHATSAPP_*
# SISTER_BASE_URL  the sister's origin this process syncs with (C12,
#                  DEPLOYMENT.md §8). The committed sisters[0].baseUrl is the
#                  sister's STAGING site, so:
#                    production  required: the sister's production origin,
#                                never sisters[0].baseUrl
#                    staging     unset (the committed staging origin), or
#                                another https origin
#                    workstation unset, or a local sister at
#                                http://localhost:<port> (plain http on
#                                loopback only)
#                  A brand with no sister ignores it, with a warning.
SISTER_BASE_URL=
# SISTER_API_KEY / SISTER_WEBHOOK_SECRET  required by bootCheck() once the
#                  brand config lists a sister (C12); 32+ characters and no
#                  development default on a deployed host
SISTER_API_KEY=
SISTER_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# --- Cache invalidation and cron (ARCHITECTURE.md §9, CONVENTIONS.md §12) ---
REVALIDATE_SECRET=dev-only-not-a-secret
CRON_SECRET=dev-only-not-a-secret

# --- Migration workstations only (MIGRATION.md) ---
# LEGACY_DATA_DIR  where the old site's raw extracts live; never committed,
#                  never set on a server
LEGACY_DATA_DIR=
